        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3ba4cc98-b080-5905-99c0-a66fee014dec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Davidson, Micajah \"Big\" Harpe, Wiley \"Little\" Harpe\n- Groups: Harpe brothers\n- Places: Stanford, Kentucky, Tennessee, Illinois, Mississippi\n- Topics: outlaw activity, first reported appearances, serial killings, highway robbery, river piracy\n\nFacts:\n- In the late eighteenth century, Micajah \"Big\" Harpe and Wiley \"Little\" Harpe operated in Tennessee, Kentucky, Illinois, and Mississippi.\n- Micajah \"Big\" Harpe, born Joshua Harper, was born before 1768, probably around 1748, and died in August 1799.\n- Wiley \"Little\" Harpe, born William Harper, was born before 1770, probably around 1750, and died on February 8, 1804.\n- The Harpe brothers were serial killers, murderers, highwaymen, and river pirates.\n- James Davidson was among the first people to report the presence of the Harpe brothers near the city of Stanford.\n- James Davidson’s report near Stanford was the Harpe brothers’ first reported appearance in Kentucky.",
